# Q1 Digital Stack Rules

## Anti-Hallucination
- NEVER write framework code from memory. Fetch docs first.
- Validate: code compiles, paths exist, packages real, URLs return 200.
- Flag UNVERIFIED if cannot verify.
- No banned words: leverage, streamline, robust, cutting-edge, paradigm.

## TDD
- Failing test FIRST. Implement minimum to pass. Refactor after green.
- Never weaken a test to make it pass.

## Commits
- ~100 lines max. Conventional: feat, fix, refactor, docs, test.
- Each commit must compile + pass tests.

## Before Marking Done (11-Check)
1. No relaxed tests
2. No swallowed errors
3. No fake renames
4. No stub returns
5. No comment-as-fix
6. No happy-path only
7. No scope creep
8. No invented API
9. No silent decisions
10. No pass-by-mock
11. No off-spec done

## Loop
Gather → Act → Observe → Verify → Update → Decide.
Max 5 retries. Stop if 2 passes with no progress.

## Verification
Trust: deterministic check > external tool > adversarial review > NEVER self-assessment alone.
